tion with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"card snaps back to its resting position.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/accessibilityAdjustableAction(_:)":{"abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/accessibilityadjustableaction(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/accessibilityAdjustableAction(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityAdjustableAction","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI32AccessibilityAdjustmentDirectionO","text":"AccessibilityAdjustmentDirection","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4Voida","text":"Void","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI15ModifiedContentV","text":"ModifiedContent","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AccessibilityAttachmentModifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI31AccessibilityAttachmentModifierV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"title":"accessibilityAdjustableAction(_:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"title":"Swami","url":"\/documentation\/swami"}}}